cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "PS5-1422-REHOST: a documented rehost of the PlayStation 5 14.22 kernel under QEMU"
abstract: >-
  The first publicly documented rehost of a current-generation console kernel on a PC:
  a genuine PlayStation 5 system-software 14.22 kernel booted under QEMU on commodity
  AMD hardware with no Sony hypervisor, to its own "Device configuration finished."
  marker, with every synthetic required registered, observable, and revertible. Includes
  the reconstruction method (remove what never runs, model what is, guards aren't inert)
  and the full analysis and boot toolchain. Distributes no firmware.
authors:
  - name: "PS5-1422-REHOST contributors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-11-21
keywords:
  - kernel rehosting
  - firmware analysis
  - QEMU
  - security research
  - PlayStation 5
license: MIT
